From: ROG5 Linux maintainers <rog5-linux@invalid>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a6xx: propagate GMU power-level probe errors

The GMU power-level setup can fail while adding the OPP table or constructing
RPMh votes.  Do not continue into ACD, HFI, and RSCC/PDC initialization with
incomplete power data.

Signed-off-by: ROG5 Linux maintainers <rog5-linux@invalid>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -2401,7 +2401,9 @@ int a6xx_gmu_init(struct a6xx_gpu *a6xx_gpu, struct device_node *node)
 	gmu->gxpd = dev_pm_domain_attach_by_name(gmu->dev, "gx");
 
 	/* Get the power levels for the GMU and GPU */
-	a6xx_gmu_pwrlevels_probe(gmu);
+	ret = a6xx_gmu_pwrlevels_probe(gmu);
+	if (ret)
+		goto detach_gxpd;
 
 	ret = a6xx_gmu_acd_probe(gmu);
 	if (ret)
-- 
2.50.1
